Give status 2 when diff cannot write its output.
diff sets its error status to 1 once its operands have been checked,
and its buffered output was written at exit without a check, so a
failed write gave status 1, which means the files differ, or was
ignored. Flush stdout at the end with an error status of 2, as GNU diff
uses for trouble.

---
 editors/diff.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -1108,5 +1108,7 @@
 			free(file[dir]);
 	}
 
-	return exit_status;
+	/* A write error is trouble, not a difference */
+	xfunc_error_retval = 2;
+	fflush_stdout_and_exit(exit_status);
 }
